{"code":"25-4012.00","title":"Curators","description":"Administer collections, such as artwork, collectibles, historic items, or scientific specimens of museums or other institutions. May conduct instructional, research, or public service activities of institution.","jobZone":5,"kinds":{"R":{"score":2.47,"share":0.0925},"I":{"score":3.43,"share":0.1528},"A":{"score":2.98,"share":0.1245},"S":{"score":3.82,"share":0.1774},"E":{"score":3.84,"share":0.1786},"C":{"score":5.36,"share":0.2742}},"highPoints":["C","E","S"],"tasks":[{"id":18641,"text":"Plan and organize the acquisition, storage, and exhibition of collections and related materials, including the selection of exhibition themes and designs, and develop or install exhibit materials.","core":true,"importance":4.35,"relevance":98.38,"frequency":3.5},{"id":1644,"text":"Develop and maintain an institution's registration, cataloging, and basic record-keeping systems, using computer databases.","core":true,"importance":4.15,"relevance":77.48,"frequency":4.08},{"id":1649,"text":"Plan and conduct special research projects in area of interest or expertise.","core":true,"importance":4.03,"relevance":94.42,"frequency":3.27},{"id":1645,"text":"Provide information from the institution's holdings to other curators and to the public.","core":true,"importance":3.94,"relevance":97.36,"frequency":3.71},{"id":1648,"text":"Negotiate and authorize purchase, sale, exchange, or loan of collections.","core":true,"importance":3.84,"relevance":90.57,"frequency":2.54},{"id":1655,"text":"Study, examine, and test acquisitions to authenticate their origin, composition, history, and to assess their current value.","core":true,"importance":3.84,"relevance":86.34,"frequency":2.87},{"id":1646,"text":"Inspect premises to assess the need for repairs and to ensure that climate and pest control issues are addressed.","core":true,"importance":3.81,"relevance":75.72,"frequency":3.07},{"id":1654,"text":"Write and review grant proposals, journal articles